$WW,1$$FG,5,0$ZealOS POSIX Compatibility Layer$FG$

$TR,"Overview"$
This is a comprehensive POSIX/libc compatibility layer for ZealOS,
enabling cross-compiled Linux/BSD programs to run on ZealOS. The goal
is to provide enough compatibility that existing software "just works"
when statically compiled for Linux x86_64.

$TR,"Components"$

$FG,2$Core POSIX Layer (/Home/POSIX/)$FG$
- MakePOSIX.ZC - Main loader for POSIX compatibility
- Process management, environment, file descriptors

$FG,2$C Standard Library (/Home/POSIX/libc/)$FG$
- stddef.h.ZC, stdint.h.ZC, limits.h.ZC - Type definitions
- string.h.ZC - String operations (strlen, strcpy, strcmp, etc.)
- stdlib.h.ZC - Memory allocation (malloc, free, realloc)
- stdio.h.ZC - File I/O (fopen, fread, fwrite, printf)
- printf.ZC - Full printf/sprintf/fprintf implementation
- unistd.h.ZC - UNIX system calls (fork, exec, pipe)
- popen.ZC - Process I/O (popen, pclose, system)
- time.ZC - Time functions (time, strftime, gettimeofday)
- math.ZC - Math library (sin, cos, tan, exp, log, sqrt)
- poll.ZC - I/O multiplexing (poll, select, epoll)
- mman.ZC - Memory mapping (mmap, munmap, mprotect)
- pthread.ZC - POSIX threads (pthread_create, mutex, cond)
- netdb.ZC - DNS resolver (getaddrinfo, gethostbyname)
- termios.ZC - Terminal I/O (tcgetattr, tcsetattr)
- curses.ZC - Curses library (initscr, newwin, addch, getch)
- pwd.ZC - User database (getpwuid, getpwnam)
- locale.ZC - Locale support (setlocale, localeconv)
- signal.ZC - Signal handling (signal, sigaction, sigsetjmp)
- regex.ZC - Regular expressions (regcomp, regexec)
- ctype.h.ZC - Character classification (isalpha, isdigit)
- errno.h.ZC - Error codes

$FG,2$C++ Runtime Support (/Home/POSIX/libc/)$FG$
- cxxabi.ZC - C++ ABI (__cxa_atexit, __cxa_guard_*, __cxa_throw)
- new.ZC - operator new/delete (throwing, nothrow, aligned)
- unwind.ZC - Stack unwinding for exceptions

$FG,2$Toolchain (/Home/POSIX/toolchain/)$FG$
- TCC.HH, TCC_OS.ZC - TinyCC compiler integration
- ELF.HH, ELFLoader.ZC - ELF binary loader (static)
- DynLink.HH, DynLink.ZC - ELF dynamic linker (shared libs)
- LibStubs.ZC - Standard library symbol stubs
- tcc.ZC - TCC command-line driver
- include/ - C standard headers for TCC

$FG,2$Go Language Support (/Home/POSIX/go/)$FG$
- Go.HH - Go runtime definitions
- Futex.ZC - Futex implementation for synchronization
- runtime/GoRuntime.ZC - M-P-G scheduler
- runtime/GoSyscall.ZC - Linux syscall emulation
- MakeGo.ZC - Go loader and command interface

$FG,2$GNU Utilities (/Home/POSIX/libc/gnu/)$FG$
- Shell utilities: sh, sed, awk, make
- File utilities: tar, gzip, cat, ls, cp, mv, rm
- Text utilities: grep, sort, head, tail, wc

$FG,2$Native Utilities (/Home/POSIX/bin/)$FG$
- wget.ZC - HTTP/HTTPS file downloader (uses native TLS)

$FG,2$Configuration (/Home/POSIX/etc/)$FG$
- lynx.cfg - Lynx browser configuration
- mime.types - MIME type mappings

$TR,"Usage"$

$FG,2$Loading the POSIX Layer:$FG$
$FG,4$
#include "/Home/POSIX/MakePOSIX"
#include "/Home/POSIX/libc/MakeLibc"
$FG$

$FG,2$Running a Cross-Compiled ELF Binary:$FG$
$FG,4$
// On Linux, compile with:
// gcc -static -o myprogram myprogram.c

// On ZealOS:
#include "/Home/POSIX/libc/MakeLibc"
ELFRun("/path/to/myprogram", argc, argv);
$FG$

$FG,2$Using Native wget:$FG$
$FG,4$
#include "/Home/POSIX/bin/MakeBin"
wget_main(2, {"wget", "https://example.com/file.zip"});
$FG$

$TR,"Supported Functionality"$

$FG,2$File I/O:$FG$
- Standard streams (stdin, stdout, stderr)
- File operations (open, close, read, write, lseek)
- Directory operations (opendir, readdir, mkdir, rmdir)
- File info (stat, fstat, access)

$FG,2$Process Management:$FG$
- fork, exec*, waitpid
- getpid, getppid, getuid, getgid
- system, popen, pclose

$FG,2$Memory:$FG$
- malloc, realloc, calloc, free
- mmap, munmap, mprotect

$FG,2$Networking:$FG$
- socket, connect, bind, listen, accept
- send, recv, sendto, recvfrom
- getaddrinfo, gethostbyname
- Native DNS resolver

$FG,2$Terminal:$FG$
- termios (tcgetattr, tcsetattr)
- curses (window management, colors, input)
- isatty, ttyname

$FG,2$Threading:$FG$
- pthread_create, pthread_join
- Mutexes, condition variables, read-write locks
- Thread-local storage

$FG,2$Signals:$FG$
- signal, sigaction
- sigsetjmp, siglongjmp
- raise, kill, alarm

$TR,"Cross-Compilation Guide"$

To run Linux programs on ZealOS:

$FG,2$1. Compile C programs statically on Linux:$FG$
$FG,4$
CFLAGS="-static" LDFLAGS="-static" ./configure
make
$FG$

$FG,2$2. Compile C++ programs statically on Linux:$FG$
$FG,4$
g++ -static -static-libgcc -static-libstdc++ -o myprogram myprogram.cpp
$FG$

$FG,2$3. For Go programs:$FG$
$FG,4$
GOOS=linux GOARCH=amd64 CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -o program
$FG$

$FG,2$4. Copy binary to ZealOS disk$FG$

$FG,2$5. Run via ELF loader:$FG$
$FG,4$
ELFRun("/path/to/program", argc, argv);
$FG$

$TR,"Running Dynamically-Linked Binaries"$

ZealOS now supports running dynamically-linked Linux binaries through
the built-in dynamic linker. This eliminates the need for static linking
in many cases.

$FG,2$Running a Dynamic Binary:$FG$
$FG,4$
#include "/Home/POSIX/toolchain/MakeToolchain"
DynRun("/path/to/program", argc, argv);
$FG$

$FG,2$Using the dlopen API:$FG$
$FG,4$
void *handle = dlopen("libfoo.so", RTLD_NOW);
if (!handle) {
    printf("Error: %s\n", dlerror());
    return -1;
}

void (*func)() = dlsym(handle, "my_function");
func();

dlclose(handle);
$FG$

$FG,2$How It Works:$FG$
The dynamic linker provides ZealOS implementations for all standard
library symbols (libc, libpthread, libm, etc.). When a binary needs
libc.so.6, the dynamic linker intercepts and provides ZealOS functions.

Supported fake libraries:
- libc.so.6 - C standard library
- libm.so.6 - Math library
- libpthread.so.0 - POSIX threads
- libdl.so.2 - Dynamic linking
- libgcc_s.so.1 - GCC runtime
- libstdc++.so.6 - C++ standard library
- libncurses.so.6 - Terminal handling

$TR,"Known Limitations"$

- Single-threaded execution (cooperative multitasking)
- Simplified signal delivery
- No /proc or /sys filesystem
- Limited ioctl support
- No SystemV IPC (shared memory, semaphores)

$TR,"Files Summary"$

Total files in POSIX layer: ~50
Total lines of code: ~15,000

Key files:
- MakePOSIX.ZC - Core POSIX initialization
- libc/MakeLibc.ZC - libc loader (includes all libc modules)
- toolchain/ELFLoader.ZC - ELF binary execution
- go/MakeGo.ZC - Go language support

